\title{Wind Curtailment and Redispatch Costs\\in the Iberian Day-Ahead Market}
\author{A.~Bondevik and L.~Marques}
\date{April 2026}

\begin{document}
\maketitle
\tableofcontents

\input{chapters/intro}
\input{chapters/context}
\input{chapters/data}
\input{chapters/findings}

\end{document}

\chapter{Findings}
Three findings stand out:
\begin{itemize}
\item curtailment is concentrated in the north-western export corridor;
\item a local market split would cut redispatch cost by a sixth;
\item dynamic line rating removes a quarter of the remaining orders.
The two rule changes interact favourably,
and their combined effect is close to additive.

